sage" dir=3D"auto"><div><p>There is no such thing as "anti-AI hype". People=
 who believe that current of GenAI is unethical are not trying to hype up a=
nything or sell you anything. Big Vim is not trying to sell you more plain =
text.</p><p>The US tech industry has been slurping up our data for a couple=
 of decades now. But in every case, they have managed to persuade enough pe=
ople that it was worth it.</p><p>A lot of people objected to their web site=
s being scraped by search engines, but the argument was that this was actua=
lly good for you, because search engines send people to you. You get the cr=
edit. Your business gets the virtual foot traffic. It's basically free targ=
eted advertising.</p><p>A lot of people objected to social media companies =
selling your interests and attention to advertisers, but the argument was t=
hat you got free access to a real service in return. All your friends are t=
here, and we give you a common place to hang out, and all we ask is for you=
r data in return.</p><p>Companies that took your data without giving you so=
mething in return, even exploiting you like Cambridge Analytica, used to be=
 considered rogue. They caused an international scandal.</p><p>Is it any su=
rprise that when Generative AI companies slurp up your data and give you no=
thing in return, people are angry? They broke the social contract that they=
 established.</p><p>Current LLM AI coding assistants, the models behind the=
m, are an unauthorised derivative work of my source code, which violate the=
 licence under which I released it. I did not agree this use of my source c=
ode. Nobody agreed to it.</p><p>Don't get me wrong, I'm not precious about =
it. I am happy for anyone to read it and learn from it. Maybe I'd feel diff=
erently if LLM models were a free public good. But I am not okay with a cor=
poration taking my work, compressing it, and selling it back.</p><p>Maybe t=
his is a weird hill to die on. Maybe I read too many cyberpunk novels in th=
e 90s which taught me that corporations which take and don't give are not y=
our friends. Maybe I'm an old man yelling at clouds. But this has crossed a=
 line for me. The mask has dropped and the rug has been pulled, and I'm not=
 taking it lying down.</p><p>Besides, even if I could overcome my conscienc=
e, I have actually read my contract, and I am not allowed to check in code =
that I didn't write and don't have a licence for.</p></div></div><span clas=
