ions.  I consider myself to fall around the 90th percentile of my graduatin=
g cohort yet it's difficult to stand out; everyone's using AI to do their c=
oursework and a disturbing amount of people are admitting to using AI in th=
e interview phase.   I've done everything right, good grades, internship at=
 a F50 company, leetcode, and as it stands with my current call back rate I=
'll be lucky to land an on premise IT support role.</p><p>I am bullish on t=
he potential of this tech but what's the point if I can't afford to partici=
