uto"><div><p>I'm very excited about what the future will bring.  I think in=
 terms of the future, the basic thing to consider is that when you make the=
 complements of something cheaper, that thing becomes cheaper.  So in the c=
ase of software, for any business that has software as a bottleneck that bu=
siness will do better, since the software is cheaper.  I am incredibly exci=
ted about the robots, which I think are the major thing coming.  I have a d=
eli/coffee shop, and there are quite a few jobs that people hate and are on=
ly done because they need money -- line cooks have a short timespan, dishwa=
shers, etc let along cleaning toilets and dumpsters and a whole bunch of st=
uff no one wants to do.  A lot of jobs will go away, but quite a few of the=
m are shit jobs.  And a lot of white collar jobs are bullshit jobs, which a=
re sort of like "why does this exist in the first place."</p><p>But outside=
 of that, we actually could do a lot more than we do now because we are so =
insanly labor constrained.  We do about 10 types of pastries a day, we coul=
d up that to 50 ahve smaller runs.  We could do custom orders better, we co=
uld handle random things, and the cost would so different.  And the humans =
would be there chilling with humans, since the actual reason people go to p=
laces like this is for the social interactions.  (I don't see a world where=
 baristas would ever go away, and I employ 6 of them.)</p><p>I'm not sure i=
f Paulo meant it in this way, but its super dangerous to say things like "T=
he only value that poor people had it was on their labor".  That's not true=
, you don't want that to be true, and you don't want to push towards a worl=
d that robs people of human dignity.</p><p>On the corporate side, I think w=
hat Marx called Wage Slaves are basically done, that whole class is going a=
way and it'll be considered a temporary situation, like building a guild me=
mber or whatever.  I believe that it will push more towards jobs that have =
a purpose, that you'll need to worry less about survival and be able to foc=
us more on being that impact you want to have in the world.  Its a hope any=
way, way too early to tell but I'm optimistic.</p></div></div><span class=
