<div><p>I think that, right now, AI code is not very high quality. But work=
s. And I think that soon it will be high quality. Indeed I think that soon =
it will move from super-junior to super-senior (exactly what happened with =
e.g. computer chess): better that what the best human would be able to do.<=
/p><p>What I find dangerous is what will probably happen now in the short t=
erm; AI right now writes code like at an amazing junior, at a tiny fraction=
 of the cost and at an impressive speed. Why would a company hire a junior =
today?</p><p>Also right now the code is so-so but the speed is incredible..=
. so we're going to get much more software of lower quality; not exactly wh=
at we needed, in my opinion. Current software is already really really (rea=
lly) bad, on average.</p></div></div><span class=3D"post-media"><ul data-ro=
