age " data-role=3D"message" dir=3D"auto"><div><p>Love how tunnel-vision mak=
es people think they figured everything out. <br>I work professionally as S=
oftware Dev for the past 20 years (25+ years if you include my side-hustle =
as a teenager in building websites for money). I've been trying a lot of di=
fferent LLMs for the past few months, and I'm hardly impressed. Every singl=
e one of them create a huge mess that I would never approve in a PR, and th=
at's even if the code actually does what is supposed to do. I thought I'm j=
ust bad at "prompting" but after consulting with many colleagues, all exper=
ienced the same thing.</p><p>Even if LLM could write perfect code every tim=
e for any size of task, The Anti-AI is not a "hype", it's actual profession=
als who understand perfectly that being a software dev is maybe 10% writing=
 code, and 9o% are soft-skills tasks that require talent, expertise and hum=
an intelligence: translating vague, ever-shifting and incoherent "Product r=
equirements" to actual concrete, deterministic and coherent architecture, a=
nd keeping it alive for many years with shifting requirements, technologies=
 and contribution by different skill-level people.</p><p>LLM works best if =
you write a small piece of code, maybe 10-15 classes max, and only in a "po=
pular" language like TypeScript, Python or Java. It is miles away from unde=
rstanding complex systems with dozens of services, written by hundreds of d=
evelopers, sometimes in different languages, with different scale / perform=
ance requirements. Even for humans, it can be extremely hard to grasp the W=
HY a system was built in a way, before they even try to understand HOW.</p>=
<p>Useful as it is once the 'honey moon phase' - where we get it essentiall=
y for free, while the leading AI companies suffer losses in the Billions - =
will be over, it will downsize to it's natural size as a useful tool in a g=
rowing toolbox. I also don't think it's worth the energy footprint on our p=
lanet. It's blockchain all over again - 5% gain for x100 the resources.</p>=
